{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1538059-homebrew-themed-cruac-sowing-blood-harvesting-coin","id":1538059,"title":"[Homebrew] [Themed Cruac] Sowing Blood / Harvesting Coin","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-07-03T14:56:26-07:00","id":1538059,"title":"[Homebrew] [Themed Cruac] Sowing Blood / Harvesting Coin","content":"<br /> To practice writting some magic, I've decided to write up two rituals... One, older rite, used for .. fertility I don't expect this one to ever be used in a game, but it's for context, as my second ritual will be &quot;inspired&quot; by this one, in universe. This is based in Blood Sorcery/ Rites of Damnation.<br /> <br /> (CW: Mentions of a womb)<br /> Sowing Blood (Creation 5)<br /> Survival of human herds is essential for the survival of Kindred. This old rite, used to be used in times of famine, or sometimes when beseeched by kine, . In order to enact the rite, the ritualist needs a woman who has never been pregnant. Some traditionalists would ask for a virgin, but that's unnecessarily. The woman's belly and womb are cut open, as she bleeds out, her body is carried encircling the fields to be blessed, her blood marking out the territory. If the woman survives, she is unable to have any offspring, similarly, she might be cut off from any magic requiring fertility. This is little known, as survival of these women was rare, and casting protection or similar magic was considered risking this ritual and would sometimes yield corrupted fruit. Her fertility acts as the sacrifice here, allowing Cruac to produce edible food.<br /> This way, witches would feed their own herds, essentially &quot;sowing&quot; so they can themselves harvest the fruits and blood of the kine living there. The field is blessed with the woman's fertility, both increasing the rate of any fruits grown there, but also increasing the size of what can be reaped. Both growth speed, and size of harvest start out at 1 of their normal rate. Alocate potency between these factors. Multiply the growth speed and size of harvest by these factors. For example, with potency 3, 2 could be allocated to speed and 1 to size, making the field grow 3 times faster and produce twice the harvest. The duration of this ritual needs to encompass the harvest of the fruit, and the size the full duration of the field.<br /> Motif (Corrupting): If a man who loves the woman performs this carrying, reduce the Risk of the ritual by 4.<br /> +3 Risk: Each point of Potency increases both the speed and size of the harvest<br /> <br /> and wrote this one, in universe inspired by the first one:<br /> Harvesting the Coin (Guidance 5)<br /> This ritual applies the ancient principles of sowing and growing ones fruit, but to the more manmande creation of coin. The modern banking, stock exchange, and similar financial instutions and mechanisms were built in such a way that one can apply some similar reasoning as farming: Investing ones time, owned resources and similar, one can expect a higher yield, or so to say harvest down the line. This ritual, mirroring an older rite, speeds up and enhances the fruit of such labor. This ritual must be performed in an instution with some form of function which allows one to invest their money and which has the potential for fast returns. This could be done in a stock exchange, or a gambling house. A person is ritually sacrificed in the premises of the establishment, his body must be cut up and distributed to cover the premises. Any targets of the ritual, gain Potency dots of Resources for the Duration, at a rate of 1 Dot per Night. Any blood, guts and gore within the space produced during this ritual are absorbed into the building over the next 3 hours. Once the Duration ends, these reappear somewhere within the building. Similarly, with the Duration of the ritual ending and resources ending, the paper trail left by these changes upon inspection might look like fraud, inside trading or the like.<br /> Add Transmutation 3: The location can be a slower institution, like a bank. The documentation is changed, and the records and bank accounts show the riches as being there and becomes fully accessible immediately after the ritual.<br /> Add Divination 2: The location or time of the body parts reappearing is known to the caster.<br /> Add Destruction 3: The body parts are gone permanently.<br /> Add Creation 3: Once the Duration of the ritual lapses, there's no mundane traces of fraud, inside trading or the like.<br /> <br /> <br /> Did some made up napkin maths for Sowing Bood just to see if things line up well: Given theme 5, Cruac here is 5, so even manip 3 / Occult 3, would give a fairly decent dice pool of 4 dice. (76% success rate), throwing in a WP for +3 (would make it a 92%). tho, taking a few more intervals of casting, which should be easy for such a ritual, would produce similar results (Thus fairly reasonably having 95%+ succ chance)<br /> <br /> If wanted, I could describe changes and target number of successes for regular core book users, needed, but I am personally looking for thoughts for these, as they are for the Theme system.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-05T15:36:04-07:00","id":1541611,"title":"","content":"Very dark rituals, but interesting. Not fit for players though, but excellent as an old Crone practice, mack guffin or plothook.<br /> <br /> The second ritual is adapted to an Invictus/Mother Army secret alliance setting, and could propel the entire plot, with one the player's friend in the local stock exchange mysteriously disappearing, and gross fragments popping in the major bank of the city after several weeks... the story spin itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26829,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26829-vumerion","user":"Vumerion","date":". 09-05-2024, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26829-vumerion","name":"Vumerion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-07T10:56:26-07:00","id":1541689,"title":"","content":"I would add a bonus to the second ritual depending on the victim :<br /> +1 dice if it works here, +2 if his/her work is important (boss)<br /> +1 to +3 dices if the victim is excellent at generating money.<br /> Or something like this.<br /> <br /> Therefor the ritual is not just &quot;killing any homeless to produce money&quot; (it could still), but &quot;kill someone important and with dire consequences, judiciary and otherwise, for a crazy shittone of money&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26829-vumerion","name":"Vumerion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-08T07:16:41-07:00","id":1541735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vumerion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1538059-homebrew-themed-cruac-sowing-blood-harvesting-coin?p=1541689#post1541689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would add a bonus to the second ritual depending on the victim :<br /> +1 dice if it works here, +2 if his/her work is important (boss)<br /> +1 to +3 dices if the victim is excellent at generating money.<br /> Or something like this.<br /> <br /> Therefor the ritual is not just &quot;killing any homeless to produce money&quot; (it could still), but &quot;kill someone important and with dire consequences, judiciary and otherwise, for a crazy shittone of money&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm defo against the idea of giving this bonuses for killing someone who works here. The ritual is, symbolically, a continuation of the first ritual. It's about improving or creating a harvest.<br /> Killing someone who works there would be like poisoning the soil and then trying to cast magic to grow something in it.<br /> <br /> Also killing someone homeless is still.. quite a thing. Whether the PCs are tasked to going and picking someone up, or if they're the ones who are happy to become serial killers of homeless people - these thing still have consequences.<br /> <br /> Will think more on picking someone good at making money and how that connects with the themes of the rituals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T01:56:58-07:00","id":1541841,"title":"","content":"I've thought about it: Bonuses for taking someone from a _competing_ organization/institution? Not only that lines up with the ritual's objectives, but also gives a trace for further plot. After all, the competing organization has reasons to believe that this organization is potentially at faults.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}